$$
2x + 3x\frac{dy}{dx} + 3y + 2y\frac{dy}{dx}
$$

Group terms:

$$
(3x + 2y)\frac{dy}{dx} + 2x + 3y = 0
$$

Solve for $ \frac{dy}{dx} $:

$$
(3x + 2y)\frac{dy}{dx} = -(2x + 3y)
$$

$$
\frac{dy}{dx} = \frac{-(2x + 3y)}{3x + 2y}
$$

---

